      "reviewLead": {
        "id": "session-usage-outcome-review-gap",
        "title": "4 long-session candidates still need outcome review",
        "reason": "4 of 12 analyzed sessions (33.3%) crossed the estimated active-time threshold; the longest estimate was 498 minutes and 0 have reviewed outcomes. 0 additional long spans may be idle or resumed work. This is an investigation lead, not a confirmed efficiency, decomposition, tool, or model problem.",
        "expectedOutcome": "Each displayed candidate is classified by task family, outcome, and friction so the report can decide whether any real improvement is needed.",
        "aiFixPrompt": "/better-harness review these sessions\n\n4 long-session candidates still need outcome review\n\n## Evidence to inspect\n\n- S1: user-thread candidate, about 498 estimated active minutes, 41 failure event(s)\n- S2: user-thread candidate, about 97.2 estimated active minutes, 9 failure event(s)\n- S3: user-thread candidate, about 80.9 estimated active minutes, 13 failure event(s)\n- S4: user-thread candidate, about 48.5 estimated active minutes, 11 failure event(s)\n\n## First step\n\nCreate <run> in the OS temporary directory, then run from the project root:\n\n```bash\nnode scripts/session-analysis.mjs insights --platform pi --workspace . --selection all-eligible --limit 1000 --format json --output <run>/insights.json\nnode scripts/session-analysis/usage-review-packet.mjs --source <run>/insights.json --workspace . --limit 8 --output <run>/.review-packet.json\n```\n\nThe private review packet resolves candidates locally. Write taskFamily, outcome, friction, confidence, and evidenceReason only for S1, S2, S3, S4. Finish diagnosis before editing product code or creating a Memory, Skill, or Hook.\n\n## What we saw\n\n4 of 12 analyzed sessions (33.3%) crossed the estimated active-time threshold; the longest estimate was 498 minutes and 0 have reviewed outcomes. 0 additional long spans may be idle or resumed work. This is an investigation lead, not a confirmed efficiency, decomposition, tool, or model problem.\n\n## Why review it\n\nWithout outcome review, complex work, tool friction, idle/resume noise, and a normal long task remain indistinguishable.\n\n## Expected result\n\nEach displayed candidate is classified by task family, outcome, and friction so the report can decide whether any real improvement is needed.\n\n## Scope\n\nCreate only a privacy-safe session-efficiency review and reader report. Do not edit product code or treat wall span as active cost. Durable reports keep aliases only; do not copy the private review packet into them. This is the complete 4/4 candidate view; conclusions still require semantic review.\n\n## Done when\n\n<run>/.review.json has one valid row for each of S1, S2, S3, S4; semantic review writes <run>/insights.reviewed.json; and <run>/report.md validates against the reviewed source. If review confirms no problem, do not create an improvement.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Run `node scripts/session-analysis/usage-semantic-review.mjs --source <run>/insights.json --packet <run>/.review-packet.json --review <run>/.review.json --output <run>/insights.reviewed.json`\n- Run `node scripts/session-analysis/validate-usage-report.mjs --source <run>/insights.reviewed.json --report <run>/report.md`; it must return `ok: true`\n- Confirm `outcomeReview.reviewedActiveLongCount` in the reviewed source equals the number of reviewed displayed aliases; delete the two private review files after validation",
        "sampleCoverage": {
          "shown": 4,
          "total": 4,
          "complete": true
